DO NOT read any files or run any commands — answer purely from this prompt; everything you need is inline. Be concise and direct.
Adversarial review of two small desk-side changes to a phone-controlled Claude Code desk (tmux-driven TUI). Answer in <=25 lines: VERDICT (SHIP / DON'T SHIP) + numbered findings with the concrete failure each causes.

Change A — interrupt honesty when an overlay is open. `POST /api/sessions/:id/interrupt` sends Escape to the pane and verifies the generation stopped by watching interrupt marks / spinner. Measured 2026-09-07 on Claude Code 2.1.263: if the `/tasks` agent panel or its detail overlay is open, one Escape only closes the overlay; the generation (and the subagent shown) keeps running, yet the desk answered "Stopped (generation confirmed stopped)." New behavior: before pressing, classify the screen; if an overlay is visible (`panel` / `detail` / `panel-empty`, detected from the region below the last `▔` separator with no composer), press Escape once, poll until no overlay is visible, and return `stopped:"overlay-closed", reason:<kind>` (phone text: "Closed the agent panel on the desk; nothing was interrupted. Tap Stop again to interrupt."); if the overlay does not disappear within the budget, return `stopped:"unverified", reason:"overlay-stuck"`. `interrupted` is true only for `verified`, unchanged. Screens without an overlay take the old path unchanged.

Change B — listing reflects a desk-confirmed stop. `GET /api/sessions/:id/subagents` derives each subagent's state from its transcript mtime (running / stalled after 15 min / finished when the parent transcript records completion). After the desk stops a subagent through the panel (`x` pressed and the panel row observed to disappear), the row still read "Working" for up to 15 minutes. New: an in-process memory (transcript path -> agentId -> time) records desk-observed stops; the listing reports `finished` with reason `stopped-by-desk` (display "Stopped") while the agent transcript has not been written after the stop time plus a 5 s grace; if the transcript moved later, the memory is ignored and mtime rules again. Parent-recorded completion outranks the memory. Entries expire after 60 min; the memory dies with the desk process.

Questions:
- A: can an overlay be misdetected (false positive) on a screen where Escape WOULD interrupt a generation, so we now under-report a real stop? Or the reverse: overlay present but undetected?
- A: after the overlay closes, the user must tap again; is there a state where the second Escape is harmful (e.g. it now interrupts the parent when the user only wanted the panel closed)?
- B: can `stopped-by-desk` be reported for an agent that is actually running (transcript writes are buffered/delayed beyond 5 s; agent that writes nothing while sleeping)?
- B: is "finished" the right state word when the desk stopped it, given counts and phone filters?
